  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 217 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA posted the propofol shortage on 2020-04-10 and it has remained on the list for 78 months as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inspection 1106244 at Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited ended 2019-09-06 and was classified OAI, with the classification letter dated 2020-05-25, 217 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the same plant on 2020-03-25, 16 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D9", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds propofol from that plant (NDC 00409469924) with 143.95 units on hand.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General also holds propofol from Pfizer Laboratories Div Pfizer Inc (NDC 00069020910) with 102.23 units on hand.",
      "cites": ["E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "P&T has approved these two NDCs as interchangeable same-product alternates.",
      "cites": ["E35"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked action is to transfer 35 units from Corvale General to Corvale Lakeside, which would give Corvale Lakeside 14 days on hand while Corvale General retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D12"]
    }
  ]
}
